1
00:00:00,933 --> 00:00:02,763
(Howard:)It's my mom's furniture.

2
00:00:02,768 --> 00:00:04,768
(Howard:)It belongs in the house
I grew up in--

3
00:00:04,770 --> 00:00:06,270
next to that pile of TV Guides

4
00:00:06,271 --> 00:00:09,271
(Howard:)and in plain view of what,
for a ten-year-old, was

5
00:00:09,274 --> 00:00:11,004
(Howard:)a quality piece
of string art!

6
00:00:14,313 --> 00:00:16,843
(Bernadette:)Howie, if the store succeeds,
Stuart has a source of income,

7
00:00:16,849 --> 00:00:19,179
(Bernadette:)and he can move out
of your mother's house.

8
00:00:19,184 --> 00:00:21,184
(Bernadette:)Seems like some old furniture
is a reasonable price

9
00:00:21,186 --> 00:00:22,316
(Bernadette:)to pay for that.

10
00:00:23,622 --> 00:00:25,022
(Howard:)That is a good point.

11
00:00:25,024 --> 00:00:26,654
(Howard:)But I didn't marry you
for good points.

12
00:00:26,659 --> 00:00:28,089
(Howard:)I married you
to blindly support me

13
00:00:28,093 --> 00:00:30,123
(Howard:)no matter how ridiculous
I'm being!

14
00:00:32,097 --> 00:00:34,297
(Bernadette:)This is why I had
to rewrite our wedding vows.

15
00:00:38,704 --> 00:00:41,934
(Leonard:)Hi, we're here to pick up
an order for Comic Center.

16
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,470
(Waitress:)Sure, let me go check on that.

17
00:00:45,110 --> 00:00:48,450
Dude, I-I think
that's Nathan Fillion.

18
00:00:49,515 --> 00:00:51,515
(Leonard:)Oh yeah,
look at that.

19
00:00:51,517 --> 00:00:53,947
(gasps) And he's picking
the tomatoes out of his salad

20
00:00:53,952 --> 00:00:55,952
(Raj:)just like I do.

21
00:00:55,954 --> 00:00:58,054
(Raj:)I always did feel
a connection with him.

22
00:00:59,958 --> 00:01:01,758
(Raj:)Oh, I have got
an idea.

